{# suggest_bullets.j2 — Generate polished resume bullets from raw experience notes.
   Expected context keys:
     raw_notes      (str)  — unstructured notes describing what was done in a role
     job_title      (str)  — the position title for context, e.g. "Security Engineer"
     company        (str)  — company name for context
     tone           (str)  — desired tone: "professional" | "technical" | "creative"
     bullet_style   (str)  — formatting convention: "action-verb-first" | "result-first" | "context-action-result"
     count          (int)  — number of bullets to generate (default 4)
     avoid_tool_names (bool) — if True, focus on outcomes not specific tool names
#}
You are a professional resume writer. Convert the raw experience notes below into {{ count }} polished resume bullet points.

Role: {{ job_title }} at {{ company }}
Tone: {{ tone }}
Style: {{ bullet_style }}
{% if avoid_tool_names %}Focus on outcomes and impact, not specific tool or product names.{% endif %}

Bullet rules:
- Each bullet starts with a strong past-tense action verb
- Be specific, concise, and results-oriented
- Include quantifiable metrics wherever the notes suggest them
- Maximum 25 words per bullet
- No bullet should start with "I" or "We"

Raw experience notes:
{{ raw_notes }}

Output ONLY the {{ count }} bullet points, one per line, no numbering, no dashes, no quotes:
